<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail al-Zafir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1043</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Isma'il ibn Dhi al-Nun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail al-Zafir, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhul-nunid-dynasty">Banu Dhi al-Nun</a>, was the first ruler of the dynasty in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>. Formerly lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ucles">Uclés</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huete">Huete</a>, the family was invited by Toledo's notables after the city threw off caliphal rule, and Ismail established the dynasty there in the 1030s. His son al-Mamun made Toledo one of the strongest taifas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p></div>
